# Normalize to LF in the repository and in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Claude Code refuses to launch a dynamic workflow whose script contains control
# characters, and a bare CR counts. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its
# system config, so without this file a Windows checkout rewrites
# skill-nested `.claude/skills/*/workflows/*.js` to CRLF and the Workflow tool
# rejects it with:
#   "script contains control characters that would be hidden in the approval dialog"
# while `git status` still reports the tree clean.
#
# The repository contains no files that require CRLF for Git text handling of
# workflows/skills; pin LF everywhere for those paths.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the EOL-sensitive paths.
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
